{
  "style": "AUDIO PROFILE: The narrator of a 90-second demo video for a command-line data tool.\nTHE SCENE: A short story about a scientist whose data migration has to match exactly, watched by engineers and scientists.\nDIRECTOR'S NOTES:\n- Style: Confident and engaged, with real tension in the problem and relief at the end. Clear, never salesy.\n- Pace: Brisk and fast, like a good trailer. Crisp consonants. Short pauses inside a sentence.\n- Accent: Neutral American English.",
  "pause": 0.28,
  "tempo": 0.97,
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "text": "Maya is moving her weather station pipeline from IDL to Python.",
      "file": "hook-8872565d3ec5.mp3",
      "seconds": 3.624,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "8105e329c8e45857d0be702c523f5874bbeda7f6058b9fb3389d80ff30f806da"
    },
    {
      "id": "parity",
      "text": "The new output has to match the old. One to one.",
      "file": "parity-353a3537b6d1.mp3",
      "seconds": 2.976,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "b12bb8e7d40cf6009aafd4c068d7bc719f0a9a1788d7f2706d753f0f0eed76e9"
    },
    {
      "id": "run",
      "text": "She runs both and compares. Every single row differs.",
      "file": "run-bbe662da9442.mp3",
      "seconds": 3.576,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "24aec5b8b3ac41343574d31058681b82ae123d4899f7423597eb2a587e8e52d4"
    },
    {
      "id": "floats",
      "text": "IDL works in 32-bit floats. Python works in 64.",
      "file": "floats-4a49846cfc43.mp3",
      "seconds": 3.528,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "e90e8034bbbf03cb9be8817d50239308f43fb01ea15352fe5c423cf778bcc727"
    },
    {
      "id": "noise",
      "text": "So the same humidity comes out two ways.",
      "file": "noise-0d860c899cae.mp3",
      "seconds": 1.872,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "b3ee694d48e287c744d09c7caeaf3db24e6ab632fb59a49412ce8d773af0121f"
    },
    {
      "id": "fill",
      "text": "IDL wrote minus 999 for a missing reading. Python writes nothing.",
      "file": "fill-7052459bd4ae.mp3",
      "seconds": 4.104,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "05f5bf77d6aad341aa92df6f8e6dacd3e092c16dd8c339a0371427e65213b71a"
    },
    {
      "id": "rename",
      "text": "She renamed temp to temperature_c, so a match by name quietly leaves it out.",
      "file": "rename-fff93b08853f.mp3",
      "seconds": 4.656,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "05c99308a6b9d33958657c7eb00f6b229ae947fee204acc320b03f9595b4d679"
    },
    {
      "id": "fix",
      "text": "And she fixed a real IDL bug. Station S3 had the wrong elevation, so its pressure changed on purpose.",
      "file": "fix-5660ea56dfd1.mp3",
      "seconds": 5.784,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "007ae45af373cd71eee85e815139008c4d609fd21ce3fd95f6b12bcce4680eed"
    },
    {
      "id": "doubt",
      "text": "Somewhere in all of that, the port has a bug of its own.",
      "file": "doubt-bdf97656f944.mp3",
      "seconds": 2.928,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "63ab47234e6ecd44c520ab7a94fa6d861080a95c116abd4fa0305af3a4381c73"
    },
    {
      "id": "question",
      "text": "Which differences are fixes, and which are corruption?",
      "file": "question-a6f87428f647.mp3",
      "seconds": 2.76,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "3fe20c0f95a384544a970c58640da6abf9586dfa3a130f32c2179f1548fd0147"
    },
    {
      "id": "reveal",
      "text": "Veridelta compares two datasets on their keys, under rules you declare.",
      "file": "reveal-295ed8053193.mp3",
      "seconds": 3.912,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "482bfc707272dd09b6a611ef4f739ffc9d62dd3294bd1d6f723a95a92a6bb92a"
    },
    {
      "id": "forgiven",
      "text": "Nothing is forgiven unless a rule says so.",
      "file": "forgiven-1bcfdc58d757.mp3",
      "seconds": 2.088,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "2bc13e7becc27225276fc8db4fcb68b64009701487afb5345da9a4fcb8498792"
    },
    {
      "id": "declare",
      "text": "Maya declares the rename. Then veridelta suggest reads the data and proposes the rest.",
      "file": "declare-07b674d71eab.mp3",
      "seconds": 4.776,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "a4b52831febc9ab23b3e2002e119a61632bf05b5a590066b77d6b9bf0f760f0e"
    },
    {
      "id": "evidence",
      "text": "One rule for humidity: a tiny tolerance, and minus 999 as missing. It explains all 124 rows.",
      "file": "evidence-4d26f79cf561.mp3",
      "seconds": 6.288,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "d93249f9ddf092906394aca32b02554a5f248802412645137dd1639fee3954da"
    },
    {
      "id": "model",
      "text": "No model is called.",
      "file": "model-da7e02dff543.mp3",
      "seconds": 0.96,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "03853737f3a5662eaf93d586982dd3aedd46e918d696a53d88cb28ea2cead0d5"
    },
    {
      "id": "baseline",
      "text": "The pressure fix was on purpose, so a baseline accepts those 31 rows. Only those.",
      "file": "baseline-32dc6645d1d3.mp3",
      "seconds": 4.536,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "1b99a1fcddadbdb53fcf6dd0d0b4db139522bd37e4b1b3a90e2f8ef712f9f39b"
    },
    {
      "id": "left",
      "text": "What's left is the real bug. Four cold readings lost their minus sign.",
      "file": "left-79791eff1cf0.mp3",
      "seconds": 3.816,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "b5fc651990f807da6bec55b12b1cee47a070e2243398c6523d380fd358d59cda"
    },
    {
      "id": "allalong",
      "text": "They were in the first rows all along.",
      "file": "allalong-0d29bc5735c4.mp3",
      "seconds": 1.368,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
      "sha256": "666bfd717b9cd3753030fff4188ab3cce1f6e6ea216f6df8f7c82173e5519249"
    },
    {
      "id": "fails",
      "text": "The run fails, and in CI, so does the pull request.",
      "file": "fails-1df4a1c3f598.mp3",
      "seconds": 2.784,
      "engine": "gemini",
      "voice": "Orus",
      "take": "f5e9a51e595b",
